{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive","id":779050,"title":"Dragonfire Mechanics (Wait, it's Reflexive?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-03T09:49:54-08:00","id":779050,"title":"Dragonfire Mechanics (Wait, it's Reflexive?)","content":"So, uh, is dragonfire supposed to be reflexive? Because the ability to breathe fire as a reflexive action seems... good. I mean, it makes sense that other 'offensive' abilities like Basilisk's Touch or Limb from Limb would be Reflexive given that their mechanical effect is to enhance something that requires an instant action (an attack in hand to hand), but this seems like it might be a bit much. Is this working as intended?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 12-03-2015, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:18:49-08:00","id":779061,"title":"","content":"*casually looks at Matt Sat-spamming his work with Dragonfire*<br /> <br /> Yeah, it works like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:25:08-08:00","id":779068,"title":"","content":"For a Dragon breathing fire is reflexive. It is done naturally and on instinct. Atavisms are a reflection of the Primordial Beast inside a character they are a physical manifestation of the true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:36:29-08:00","id":779077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=779068#post779068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Dragon breathing fire is reflexive. It is done naturally and on instinct. Atavisms are a reflection of the Primordial Beast inside a character they are a physical manifestation of the true nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that actually is the case, it is definitely, um, 'points efficient.' Particularly when dealing with anything that is not outright immune to fire. Even worse if they are particularly vulnerable to it. &quot;Screw you, vampires! Screw you, prometheans! I'm gonna breath fire on ALL OF YOU! What's that? You're not immune to fire like a Beast with Dragonfire is? Sucks to be you, I guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bonus points for breathing fire reflexively and then shooting the target with an actual flamethrower. (Yo dawg, I heard you liked fire...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 12-03-2015, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T10:45:48-08:00","id":779080,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my biggest complaint is that it seems to screw with the action economy and 2E's tacit &quot;No multiple attacks&quot; policy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:17:21-08:00","id":779104,"title":"","content":"There is an entire thread on manifesting as your horror in this sub forum. The atavisms in my thoughts is a nice balance. While the area attack does mess with the no multiple attack policy it also establishes a Beast as something and someone to be feared.<br /> <br /> I'm the Prince of this city you ignorant child. And my word is law now escort this thing from my sight.<br /> Whoosh and roar of flame. Now your an ash heap. Now then can we all play nice or do I need to burn down another nightclub?<br /> <br /> It also helps deal with the unruly band of followers that always accompany heroes or as I think of them red shirts.<br /> <br /> If you as a Storyteller think it is too much as a reflexive action, then house rule it. I think it is in line with the theme and spirit of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:36:08-08:00","id":779125,"title":"","content":"Say, is there a limit on how many times you can take the same reflexive action in a turn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:42:16-08:00","id":779129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=779104#post779104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an entire thread on manifesting as your horror in this sub forum. The atavisms in my thoughts is a nice balance. While the area attack does mess with the no multiple attack policy it also establishes a Beast as something and someone to be feared.<br /> <br /> I'm the Prince of this city you ignorant child. And my word is law now escort this thing from my sight.<br /> Whoosh and roar of flame. Now your an ash heap. Now then can we all play nice or do I need to burn down another nightclub?<br /> <br /> It also helps deal with the unruly band of followers that always accompany heroes or as I think of them red shirts.<br /> <br /> If you as a Storyteller think it is too much as a reflexive action, then house rule it. I think it is in line with the theme and spirit of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with attacking multiple targets in the same turn, I'm talking about it turning into a D&amp;D dragon's attack routine: &quot;I use Dragonfire and then attack!&quot;<br /> <br /> Just thought that the devs were trying to adhere to a really strict action economy is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:07:23-08:00","id":779151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=779129#post779129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine with attacking multiple targets in the same turn, I'm talking about it turning into a D&amp;D dragon's attack routine: &quot;I use Dragonfire and then attack!&quot;<br /> <br /> Just thought that the devs were trying to adhere to a really strict action economy is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's worse than that. Can't you take basically as many reflexive actions per turn as you want? <br /> &quot;You can take a reflexive action at any time, and it doesn\u2019t take your turn in combat.&quot; - Beast: the Primordial, pg. 158<br /> <br /> So I, uh, hit you with infinite dragonfire attacks? Well, okay, not infinite. I can only hit you with infinite attacks if you are also immune to fire. But I hit you with whatever finite number of attacks are needed to kill you. Also, I do it on your turn, because &quot;you can take a reflexive action at any time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:24:24-08:00","id":779170,"title":"","content":"Isn't it Reflexive to summon it, then an Instant action to attack, much like Incendiary from DtD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:48:15-08:00","id":779197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=779170#post779170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it Reflexive to summon it, then an Instant action to attack, much like Incendiary from DtD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I can see. RAW, you breathe fire as a reflexive action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:37:03-08:00","id":779354,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that all this is still before the final book comes out. Even Werewolf the Forsaken went on some changes between the early release and final version. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T22:05:25-08:00","id":779543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast, pp. 122, &quot;Chapter 3: Characters and Traits,&quot; Atavisms, &quot;Systems&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many Atavisms resemble Merits in that they have persistent effects that need not be activated, such as modifying other actions or dice pools, or <b>they confer abilities that are available at no cost, such as a special attack form. Dice rolls are rarely required. When they are, they are usually reflexive and folded into another action such an attack</b>. An Atavism\u2019s dice pool always consists of an Attribute plus a Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Activating the Power is, BLAMMing someone with it is not. It still uses an attack action, as written in the systems section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T22:42:23-08:00","id":779560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=779543#post779543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Activating the Power is, BLAMMing someone with it is not. It still uses an attack action, as written in the systems section.</div> </div> </div> </div>This line of reasoning works very well for Atavisms such as Gorgon's Touch, which actually specifically states that, &quot;applying the poison requires a touch attack, but activating the Atavism itself is reflexive.&quot;<br /> <br /> Step 1: Reflexively make your touch poisonous.<br /> Step 2: touch someone.<br /> <br /> Both steps are explicitly spelled out in the rules text of the Atavism in question. In the case of Dragonfire, however, there is no step between activating the power and blamming someone with it. Nowhere is there any suggestion that you must reflexively charge your breath in order to then breathe fire. You just breathe fire. The Dragonfire Atavism *is* the attack. Which is reflexive. And counts as a ranged attack with a thrown weapon, and requires a roll of Dex + Athletics - opponent's defense. Yes, all other instances of the ranged attack action require instant actions. This one, because of the way it is written and because it is defined as a reflexive action, does not.<br /> <br /> There are other Atavisms that follow the same pattern as Dragonfire. All of the others are Instant. Compare Dragonfire to Storm-Lashed, for example. Storm-Lashed is Instant, as it should be. It grants you access to a whole bunch of special attack modes and other useful actions, ranging from 'fun things to do with sand and the eyes of your enemies' to 'summon supernaturally violent storm from which you can call down lightning bolts to murder your enemies.' Aside from the passive immunity to weather effects that the Atavism provides, all of the various applications of it are instant actions. As they should be. As dragonfire should be.<br /> <br /> I am not arguing that this is a good thing. I think this is silly and should be fixed -- either before the game goes to print or in its first errata. Yes, granted, no sane GM would ever allow you to do it the way that the rules actually say you can do it. But that doesn't change the fact that the rules are written that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 12-04-2015, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T05:27:04-08:00","id":779723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=779560#post779560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This line of reasoning works very well for Atavisms such as Gorgon's Touch, which actually specifically states that, &quot;applying the poison requires a touch attack, but activating the Atavism itself is reflexive.&quot;<br /> <br /> Step 1: Reflexively make your touch poisonous.<br /> Step 2: touch someone.<br /> <br /> Both steps are explicitly spelled out in the rules text of the Atavism in question. In the case of Dragonfire, however, there is no step between activating the power and blamming someone with it. Nowhere is there any suggestion that you must reflexively charge your breath in order to then breathe fire.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;The Beast can blast individual targets in range (5/10/15) with gouts of fire.<i><u><b> This counts as a ranged attack with a thrown weapon and requires a roll of Dexterity + Athletics \u2013 the opponent\u2019s Defense.</b></u></i> Damage is lethal and adds the Beast\u2019s Lair dots as a weapon modifier.&quot; BtP Chapter 3 p78 (emphasis mine).<br /> <br /> All attacks are instant actions. I think the intent here is that the Reflexive is to gain the ability to breath fire, then an Instant action to make a ranged attack. Perfectly valid way to read the power in question, it makes reasonable sense to me, and it is consistant with how Basilisk's Touch works. So, I'm going with this. <br /> <br /> If you want to insist that the only way to read the power is as a Reflexive attack... then just make a houserule to make it Instant. I don't really understand why we're arguing about this - if its a problem, we can fix it. Assume its a typo, assume that we're dealing with it as I'm describing, or free fireblasts that needs a fix. Easy enough to deal with all of them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are other Atavisms that follow the same pattern as Dragonfire. All of the others are Instant. Compare Dragonfire to Storm-Lashed, for example. Storm-Lashed is Instant, as it should be. It grants you access to a whole bunch of special attack modes and other useful actions, ranging from 'fun things to do with sand and the eyes of your enemies' to 'summon supernaturally violent storm from which you can call down lightning bolts to murder your enemies.' Aside from the passive immunity to weather effects that the Atavism provides, all of the various applications of it are instant actions. As they should be. As dragonfire should be. </div> </div> </div> Storm-Lashed also doesn't talk about making ranged attacks, which is a rather important thing. Basilisk's Touch requires touch attack, Dragonfire requires ranged attack, Storm-Lashed requires its own special actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:52:45-08:00","id":780001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=779723#post779723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;The Beast can blast individual targets in range (5/10/15) with gouts of fire.<i><u><b> This counts as a ranged attack with a thrown weapon and requires a roll of Dexterity + Athletics \u2013 the opponent\u2019s Defense.</b></u></i> Damage is lethal and adds the Beast\u2019s Lair dots as a weapon modifier.&quot; BtP Chapter 3 p78 (emphasis mine).<br /> <br /> All attacks are instant actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, at no point in Beast: the Primordial are attacks ever defined as being instant actions. What the rules presented in Beast actually say are: &quot;On your turn, your character can attack using one of the following dice pools...&quot; &quot;...Resolve the attack roll like any other action. Determine damage by adding the successes rolled to any weapon bonus...\u201d This is another thing that should be corrected at some point. If the Beast book is supposed to include all the rules necessary to play the game, then a statement that making an attack is an instant action should be included in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the intent here is that the Reflexive is to gain the ability to breath fire, then an Instant action to make a ranged attack. Perfectly valid way to read the power in question, it makes reasonable sense to me, and it is consistant with how Basilisk's Touch works. So, I'm going with this. </div> </div> </div>This is not what the power says. At no point in the actual text of the power is there any suggestion that the power is divided into the steps you describe (step 1, reflexively gain the ability, step 2, use an instant action to make a ranged attack). These two steps ARE described in the text of Basilisk's Touch as a means of spelling out the fact that the Atavism only makes your touch poisonous, but Dragonfire is clearly not of the same kind of atavism as Basilisk's touch. Basilisk's Touch enhances attacks you are already making. It makes your touch poisonous. It is of the same kind as Limb from Limb and Cyclopean Strength, which also enhance actions you are already making.<br /> <br /> Dragonfire, on the other hand, is the ability to breathe fire. Breathing fire counts as a ranged attack. It is of the same kind as Titanic Blow, which is the ability to make titanic blows that destroy objects (which requires a Strength + Brawl roll to hit, and is identified as an attack in the following text: &quot;her attack ignores an amount of object durability...&quot; There is no need for superfluous rules text here of the type you have described (and which are absent in the actual text), which, as near as I can tell, translate to, &quot;this Atavism reflexively gives you the ability to use this Atavism.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to insist that the only way to read the power is as a Reflexive attack... </div> </div> </div>I do not want to insist upon this, but it is, in fact, what the power says. It is obviously not what was intended, should never be allowed to work like that, and should be changed immediately, but it <b>IS</b> what the writers actually wrote. Why I suspect this happened is that the Dragonfire Atavism also includes an immunity to fire, heat, and smoke, and that part of the power is and should be reflexive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storm-Lashed also doesn't talk about making ranged attacks, which is a rather important thing. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it does. Calling down lightning is defined as being a ranged attack, and Sand in the Eyes says that, &quot;This ability causes no damage, but a successful attack applies the Blinded Tilt...&quot; Knock Back should probably be defined in its rules text as a ranged attack as well, but isn't explicitly labelled one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basilisk's Touch requires touch attack, Dragonfire requires ranged attack, </div> </div> </div>'COUNTS AS' a ranged attack. Not 'requires.' There is an important distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 12-04-2015, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T01:02:51-08:00","id":780443,"title":"","content":"Attacks are essentially Instant actions, as they take up your turn in combat, as explained in the definition of Instant actions, in the Actions section of chapter 4, and the Combat section of Chapter 4. Can you not accept an explanation that allays your concerns that a power <i>might </i>be broken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T03:17:25-08:00","id":780471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=780001#post780001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not want to insist upon this,</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that is exactly what you are doing. Insisting. You've been given several explanations that allay your fears, but you're rejecting them. I would say that the World of Darkness isn't D&amp;D, but even D&amp;D has moved away from hard, strictly defined technical rules and are encouraging more natural languages, authorial intent and individual rulings on how powers work in individual games over worrying about using highly technical and restrictive language. The WoD is writen by people who want to tell stories, not run a war game like Warhammer 40K. The rules are written for narrative impact, and sometimes they come across as something different than intended. Hell, I even pointed out that you could just make a house rule, and bam, all problems solved. Why not just go with that if you're absolutely married to the idea of it always being reflexive? <br /> <br /> I don't know why you are so insistant upon your interpretation of the rules being exclusively right when it creates a situation that doesn't make sense. There's no point to continue this other than to prove one &quot;side&quot; right or wrong. We're dealing with a pre-release draft that may change, you've been given alternative interpretations of the rules, and suggestions to just house rule things differently if you have players trying to insist on being mechanically broken. So, lets all relax and game on with whatever makes the most sense for the stories we tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T10:37:19-08:00","id":780614,"title":"","content":"I'm an editor by training; maybe that just makes me overly sensitive to the actual words used. If you want to write in natural language, that's fine, but you still have to make sure that your rules are written clearly and accurately within that context. Assumptions of authorial intent only go so far. e.g.: If the author meant 'successes are halved,' but accidentally wrote, 'successes are doubled,' that's a problem. Maybe in such a situation the readers can figure out what the author actually meant to say, but they shouldn't have to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=780471#post780471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why you are so insistant upon your interpretation of the rules being exclusively right when it creates a situation that doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the purpose of having rules is to get everyone on the same sheet of music. It is to prevent, &quot;I shot you!&quot; &quot;No you didn't!&quot; situations. Of <i>course</i> it's wrong to run it the way I have described. Of <i>course</i> it doesn't make sense. I am not trying to say that it is or should be the way I have described. It isn't and it shouldn't be. What I <i>am</i> saying is that there's a misprint in the book that we missed in the Backer proofing process, and I don't understand why there's so much resistance to the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":8950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","user":"Vithrir","date":". 12-05-2015, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T10:53:30-08:00","id":780617,"title":"","content":"The fire breathing counts as a thrown attack. Either it's instant, or all thrown attacks are reflexive, in which case it's not broken because the beast will just die under a counter hail of throwing knives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:36:07-08:00","id":780638,"title":"","content":"I think the point Vithrir is trying to make is that this ambiguity shouldn't exist. Rules should be clear and concise, there should be no room for differing takes on the rules as written.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T12:16:52-08:00","id":780653,"title":"","content":"There <i>isn't</i> room. He's somehow squeezed himself in there like some sort of contortionist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T12:39:30-08:00","id":780664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=780614#post780614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm an editor by training; maybe that just makes me overly sensitive to the actual words used. If you want to write in natural language, that's fine, but you still have to make sure that your rules are written clearly and accurately within that context.</div> </div> </div> </div> I said it before, I'll say it again. Free preview draft pdf != final product. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because the purpose of having rules is to get everyone on the same sheet of music. </div> </div> </div> Then, when you sit down at your table, tell everyone that's how you're running things. Or get the ST to make the rule if you're a player. That way, everyone is on the same page at your table, and tables are all that matter, not some world wide secret fun police. That's why I say to make either a call, or a house rule. Or wait for the final edition to come out/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T16:44:41-08:00","id":783750,"title":"","content":"The way I read it is that calling up the fire is a Reflexive action, sure, but making an attack is, as per usual, an Instant Action.<br /> <br /> In the Systems section of Atavisms, it mentions that &quot;...or they confer abilities that are available at no cost, <i>such as a special attack form</i>,&quot; (emphasis mine), &quot;Dice rolls are rarely required. When they are, they are usually reflexive and folded into another action such as an attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it's explained just fine right there, but YMMV, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T02:25:57-08:00","id":790160,"title":"","content":"I'd like a second opinion make sure I'm not alone in this interpretation before it comes up. According to the description* on Dragonfire a Beast with it does not suffer damage from fire. So that's all fire that isn't somehow augmented or something to bypass the immunity? I mean like this isn't just you'll be fine if the building you're in catches fire or you fall into a campfire this is like someone turns a flamethrower on you and the biggest issue will be that your outfit is gone. That accurate?<br /> <br /> <br /> *Spoilered the part that makes me think that here to save time on looking it up:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pg 124</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, fire causes no damage to the Beast, and she never suffers environmental penalties or damage caused by heat and smoke, which are like clear air to her.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T04:06:39-08:00","id":790202,"title":"","content":"Where does it say that you get to bypass the immunity even if its a mage throwing a magical fireball? As far as I'm aware, being immune applies there too, correct me if I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> Anyways, yes. You shrug off anything related to pain from fire. So, campfire, flamethrower, house on fire, volcano, etc won't affect you. The smoke and toxins in the area won't affect you. The burning house could start falling apart, and the falling timber could hurt you. Flame thrower could cause explosions and shrapnel hurt you. But direct fire and smoke and sulfer won't affect your health in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Immunities are a thing with Beasts. With the right set of abilities, they can shrug off a lot of tilts, both personal and environmental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-21-2015, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:29:06-08:00","id":790340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=790202#post790202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it say that you get to bypass the immunity even if its a mage throwing a magical fireball? As far as I'm aware, being immune applies there too, correct me if I'm wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>More of an ST thing of where they say there's something about the fire that makes it so your immunity doesn't apply like it normally would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:33:56-08:00","id":790455,"title":"","content":"Well, as far as mages go if they can throw a fireball they can throw a lightning bolt, so it's just a question of right tool for the job there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:03:31-08:00","id":808261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=790160#post790160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a second opinion make sure I'm not alone in this interpretation before it comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. As written you're immune to any effect that generates fire, magical or not, and can make a reflexive flamethrower attack each round in addition to your normal instant action. This allows you to do exactly what was suggested previously: buy an agragrian, build a homebrew, or steal a military flamethrower and combine it with Dragonfire to make two area flame attacks each turn, being completely immune to the immediate consequences.<br /> <br /> Setting things on fire isn't really subtle, but there's lots of times you'll probably be okay with ditching subtlety for more dakka, and the complete absence of the usual issues with, say, filling a vampire's basement with incendiaries while you're there goes a long way to make up for any later hassle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-13-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T19:50:07-08:00","id":810028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=808261#post808261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. As written you're immune to any effect that generates fire, magical or not, and can make a reflexive flamethrower attack each round in addition to your normal instant action. This allows you to do exactly what was suggested previously: buy an agragrian, build a homebrew, or steal a military flamethrower and combine it with Dragonfire to make two area flame attacks each turn, being completely immune to the immediate consequences.<br /> <br /> Setting things on fire isn't really subtle, but there's lots of times you'll probably be okay with ditching subtlety for more dakka, and the complete absence of the usual issues with, say, filling a vampire's basement with incendiaries while you're there goes a long way to make up for any later hassle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait...By it's own text doesn't it say &quot;this counts as a is a Ranged Attack with a thrown weapon&quot; thus consuming your attack action? That would negate your ability to also fire a flame thrower on that turn wouldn't it? Because you already used your 1 attack that turn? Because it counted as a &quot;Ranged Attack&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:30:45-08:00","id":810048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810028#post810028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait...By it's own text doesn't it say &quot;this counts as a is a Ranged Attack with a thrown weapon&quot; thus consuming your attack action? That would negate your ability to also fire a flame thrower on that turn wouldn't it? Because you already used your 1 attack that turn? Because it counted as a &quot;Ranged Attack&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. There's nothing that limits how many ranged or other attacks you can make - except your available actions. An &quot;attack&quot; is just a class of action that's normally instant (and thus once per turn, for the sole reason that you only have one instant action). Dragonfire is just a reflexive action that is also a ranged attack; you can take any instant action desired in addition to Dragonfire, including firing a gun, swinging a sword, disarming a bomb, whatever's salient. Nothing you can do reflexively negates your ability to act on your turn unless it explicitly says something like &quot;you can't take an action on your next turn,&quot; for example, Celerity in Vampire: the Requiem 2nd Edition. Like Dragonfire, it allows you to act reflexively, but it also specifically notes that this eats your turn.<br /> <br /> Being able to breath fire reflexively is pretty insane, but so are most Beast powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-15-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:38:54-08:00","id":810050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810048#post810048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. There's nothing that limits how many ranged or other attacks you can make - except your available actions. An &quot;attack&quot; is just a class of action that's normally instant (and thus once per turn, for the sole reason that you only have one instant action). Dragonfire is just a reflexive action that is also a ranged attack; you can take any instant action desired in addition to Dragonfire, including firing a gun, swinging a sword, disarming a bomb, whatever's salient. Nothing you can do reflexively negates your ability to act on your turn unless it explicitly says something like &quot;you can't take an action on your next turn,&quot; for example, Celerity in Vampire: the Requiem 2nd Edition. Like Dragonfire, it allows you to act reflexively, but it also specifically notes that this eats your turn.<br /> <br /> Being able to breath fire reflexively is pretty insane, but so are most Beast powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>But nothing in Dragon Fire's wording calls it out as specifically reflexive and instead seems to call it out as just another ranged attack which by the general rule is an instant action. Wouldn't the general rule take precedence here, thus making the breathing attack with your dragon fire an instant action and not reflexive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:42:48-08:00","id":810052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810050#post810050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But nothing in Dragon Fire's wording calls it out as specifically reflexive and instead seems to call it out as just another ranged attack which by the general rule is an instant action. Wouldn't the general rule take precedence here, thus making the breathing attack with your dragon fire an instant action and not reflexive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you working from an earlier version? In the backer PDF, Dragonfire is explicitly a reflexive action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:48:53-08:00","id":810058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810052#post810052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you working from an earlier version? In the backer PDF, Dragonfire is explicitly a reflexive action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was. I honestly Haven't played from the backer version and just read it over once. give me 5 minutes to read over backer version for clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:57:16-08:00","id":810060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810052#post810052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you working from an earlier version? In the backer PDF, Dragonfire is explicitly a reflexive action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright after examining the exact text which I included in the spoiler tag..<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast the Primordial Page 124</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Normal Effect: </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Dragons delight in fear and destruction, both of which are always near at hand. The Beast need only open her jaws and unleash the hellfire building within her, and a curl of smoke or a dreadful gleam in her eyes is often her victim\u2019s only warning. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">The Beast can blast individual targets in range (5/10/15) with gouts of fire. This counts as a ranged attack with a thrown </span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">weapon and requires a roll of Dexterity + Athletics \u2013 the opponent\u2019s Defense. Damage is lethal and adds the Beast\u2019s Lair dots as a weapon modifier. Flammable materials ignite on contact, turning the area into a raging inferno if it is not contained quickly. Then again, that may be the point.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">Furthermore, fire causes no damage to the Beast, and she never suffers environmental penalties or damage caused by heat and smoke, which are like clear air to her. This is in addition to any environmental immunity from Lair Traits</span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">(see p. 101)</span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">. </span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I see no specific reference to a reflexive action in this text but I do see a specific reference to counts as a ranged attack with a thrown weapon. This is a specific reference which trumps the general reference of Atavism use being reflexive. Thus the attack generated by this would be logically just another attack with a thrown weapon, and thus a instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":".  removing color tags for improved readability. 01-15-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T21:08:48-08:00","id":810066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810060#post810060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no specific reference to a reflexive action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er...did you miss the part just a few lines above, that says in bold <b>Action:</b> Reflexive?<br /> <br /> That...that'd be the action type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-16-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T21:14:15-08:00","id":810068,"title":"","content":"Sadly I did not see it, wasn't used to the formatting at the time I read that. I'm mainly an Exalted player, I've been fighting against referring to this as a charm. Thank you for calling that out I can see that now. And I suddenly see the point. I think as an ST I would probably limit this to once per turn, so that it doesn't become drastically over powered, but yes defiantly could be put into a combo with a standard attack action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T21:21:07-08:00","id":810072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810068#post810068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly I did not see it, wasn't used to the formatting at the time I read that. I'm mainly an Exalted player, I've been fighting against referring to this as a charm. Thank you for calling that out I can see that now. And I suddenly see the point. I think as an ST I would probably limit this to once per turn, so that it doesn't become drastically over powered, but yes defiantly could be put into a combo with a standard attack action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. As a note, Siren's Treacherous Song a little ways down is similar - gives you the ability to make an unusual attack - but mentions both in the <b>Action</b> line and the description of the effect that it is an instant action. Chronicles of Darkness in general has been fairly conscientious about what kind of thing is what kind of action, possibly because the New World of Darkness was not always so clear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It definitely should be limited to once a turn. To be fair, it probably SHOULD be an instant action because C of D has tried so hard to purge the dark spectre multiple attacks put over combat in the New World of Darkness, but on the other hand Beast powers are so overwhelmingly strong it's like, how much does it really matter. A Beast that means to kill a normal human will generally not find doing so troublesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T21:55:45-08:00","id":810082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810066#post810066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er...did you miss the part just a few lines above, that says in bold <b>Action:</b> Reflexive?<br /> <br /> That...that'd be the action type.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the Action type of activating Dragonfire, making the power available for yourself to use. And thereafter, you're able to make an instant action that is a Thrown attack where you spit out fire.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition has strongly been moving away with granting extra combat actions, and therefore it wouldn't make sense to be able to do Reflexive attacks that can occur as many times as you want in a single turn. Because... you can't really beat that. You just repetitively make Dragonfire reflexive attacks until the target is dead, never granting your target the opportunity to use their turn. That interpretation isn't just OP, it's broken and dysfunctional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T08:15:52-08:00","id":810231,"title":"","content":"Well, this discussion seems to be going in circles. Last time I saw it, the deal was: Activating the capacity to shoot fire = reflexive. Actually attacking with it = Instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T13:26:40-08:00","id":810336,"title":"","content":"I think the reason it's reflexive is to trigger the fire/smoke immunity and (I would argue) the capacity to shoot fire as an instant action. While the text could definately easily be read to give the player unlimited reflexive attacks, I *highly* recommend against allowing any at your table. It can't be Action: Instant because then the reflexive fire immunity wouldn't be a thing.<br /> <br /> Really this could all be solved by adding &quot;as an instant action&quot; after &quot;with gouts of fire.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T19:28:02-08:00","id":810448,"title":"","content":"One thing is certain, regardless of the level of editorial attention this gets: <b>no one I'm playing with is getting infinite reflexives, especially infinite, reflexive flamethrower attacks.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T21:18:55-08:00","id":810483,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it if it would make for an awesome scene.<br /> <br /> You can bet such a scene would also involve blowing their entire load of Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T23:04:08-08:00","id":810500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810231#post810231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this discussion seems to be going in circles. Last time I saw it, the deal was: Activating the capacity to shoot fire = reflexive. Actually attacking with it = Instant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, Siren's Treacherous Song is just a few pages down, where they specifically call it out as an instant action twice - both in the action line, and again when describing the attack, as an instant action.<br /> <br /> The confusion stems from a continued misreading of the phrase &quot;counts as a ranged attack&quot; which people are appending an extra meaning of &quot;and is also, in addition to counting as a ranged attack, an instant action.&quot; COUNTING AS a ranged attack just means that for the purpose of rules that interact with ranged attacks, it is one. Have a power that makes you immune to ranged attacks? Calculating the multiple attacker penalty and want to know if Dragonfire is the same as swinging a knife? Environmental factors levy a penalty to ranged attacks? Et cetera.<br /> <br /> Ranged attack is a status normally applied to an instant action. In this case, it's applied to a reflexive action. &quot;Ranged attack&quot; is not a quality that dictates action type.<br /> <br /> It's definitely not a case of &quot;you use the power reflexively for free, and then make an attack as an instant action.&quot; For one thing, that's incoherent, why would using the power need any action at all if it's a &quot;free&quot; action that does nothing? There's a line for that, it's called <b>Action:</b> None, which WoD has been using for passive effects since last edition. For another thing, &quot;counts as a ranged attack&quot; points at the activation of the power, which is reflexive. You'd need to have an instant action in the text to point at. Spending a free action that just says &quot;you can take another type of action now&quot; is definitely not a reasonable read, and given that the fire immunity has no duration, activating it reflexively still doesn't make sense. How long are you immune to fire? The instant you activate it, helping you exactly never? One turn? Until you say you're not? What happens if you go to sleep? Et cetera. That's a passive effect. The reflexive activation is the ranged attack.<br /> <br /> The only reason I think people are arguing so strongly for &quot;counts as&quot; to translate differently is because there's a general feeling that this definitely SHOULD be an instant action, and I agree, it should be changed, reflexive attacks are BS. Especially when they're ranged, deal agg, are good for traceless arson (this comes up every game I have ever played), and also happen to make you immune to fire in the bargain.<br /> <br /> But that's a rules change, not a typo issue, and gets into the greater conversation of &quot;do Beasts push the upper boundary of the system beyond tolerance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ideally a dev'll pop in and be like &quot;yeah, it's reflexive, but maybe that wasn't a great idea, so we're gonna make it instant&quot; as a result of this conversation, which is my sole motivation for continuing it.<br /> <br /> Also the issue of &quot;how many times can you make the same reflexive action in a turn&quot; really needs an explicit callout of &quot;exactly once&quot; in every core rulebook. That's beyond Dragonfire and comes up plenty with other reflexive powers, and while the common sense ruling is obviously once there needs to be no ambiguity there. To be 100% clear I would never argue for any RAI allowing infinite attacks because I don't think anyone has ever intended that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-17-2016, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T23:23:21-08:00","id":810503,"title":"","content":"Because if activating the power wasn't reflexive, it'd burn your action just to activate it, in which your awe inspiring Beast would be merely posing like in a Super Sentai show prior to an attack.<br /> <br /> No, it doesn't reads &quot;Obliterate everything in front, besides and behind you&quot;. That's what it'd mean if you could use that shit infinite times per turn. Fuck that.<br /> <br /> Finally, on reflexive actions. Noticing things is reflexive. Breathing is reflexive. Sweating is reflexive. Walking is reflexive too. Do you really think it'd be smart to limit those to once per turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-17-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T01:11:26-08:00","id":810527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810503#post810503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if activating the power wasn't reflexive, it'd burn your action just to activate it, in which your awe inspiring Beast would be merely posing like in a Super Sentai show prior to an attack.<br /> <br /> No, it doesn't reads &quot;Obliterate everything in front, besides and behind you&quot;. That's what it'd mean if you could use that shit infinite times per turn. Fuck that.<br /> <br /> Finally, on reflexive actions. Noticing things is reflexive. Breathing is reflexive. Sweating is reflexive. Walking is reflexive too. Do you really think it'd be smart to limit those to once per turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once per kind of reflexive action, within the limits of what could reasonably be achieved within an approximate 3 second time frame, yes. (We are keeping track of bodily functions within the combat round action economy now?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) I would argue that if the complexity of your actions for a turn take more than a minute to describe out of character, baring indecisiveness or personal issues, then you are probably trying to do to much in a single turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T01:59:53-08:00","id":810539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810527#post810527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once per kind of reflexive action, within the limits of what could reasonably be achieved within an approximate 3 second time frame, yes. (We are keeping track of bodily functions within the combat round action economy now?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) I would argue that if the complexity of your actions for a turn take more than a minute to describe out of character, baring indecisiveness or personal issues, then you are probably trying to do to much in a single turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means I can't resist two supernatural powers thrown at me on the same round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T02:35:17-08:00","id":810550,"title":"","content":"Reflexive actions are explicitly not supposed to be once per turn, even the same action. When that's supposed to be the case, the books say so, or make it so via other rules (such as linking the reflexive to an instant action).<br /> <br /> The issue with Dragonfire isn't how the core rules handle Reflexive actions, but the wording in the specific power not be clear enough for some people (even if it seems we all agree on how it is supposed to work anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:07:40-08:00","id":810628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810503#post810503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if activating the power wasn't reflexive, it'd burn your action just to activate it, in which your awe inspiring Beast would be merely posing like in a Super Sentai show prior to an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>If activating the power was instant, then you would breathe fire as an instant action. The activation of the power <i>does not</i>, unlike, again, <i>later available examples</i>, provide the ability to make an attack. The activation of the power IS an attack, which is why it counts as a ranged attack, instead of - the wording you'd need for your interpretation - granting you the ability to make an attack as an instant action.<br /> <br /> It doesn't say that and it isn't meant to say that.<br /> <br /> Breathing and sweating aren't actions any more than being alive is an action. I don't ask my players to write down a list of autonomic body functions as their reflexive action for the turn and then blind them if they forgot to mention &quot;using my eyes to interpret visual data&quot; which is where you seem to be heading. Walking is movement, and movement, yes, has limitations attached. You're not limited by how many times you can resist supernatural powers, and you can't resist the same power fifty times in a turn until you succeed your roll. This is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> But if reflexives were infinite, most Beast powers have a serious problem. Does Needs Must add my Lair dots to my Perception, or an infinite amount of multiples of my Lair dots since I can keep activating it freely? Actually...why isn't that <b>Action:</b> None? I just realized every single Atavism is framed as either Reflexive or Instant, and the reflexives include clearly passive effects and bonuses. But passive effects aren't activated reflexively, they're passive. It looks like maybe this is a typo issue after all, because (by your logic) you should be able to activate any of these an infinite number of times, right? Which cannot possibly be argued to be INTENT.<br /> <br /> Either this is just action mislabeling across the board or you shouldn't be able to use the same reflexive action again and again and again and again.<br /> <br /> But I think we can all agree there's a serious problem here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T11:59:40-08:00","id":810719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810539#post810539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That means I can't resist two supernatural powers thrown at me on the same round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, because tanking Supernatural Powers isn't really an active response, so I'd let you do that as often as you need to. The problem is active reflexive actions, like activating powers. Remember: I said that it had to <i>reasonably </i>fit within an approximately 3 second long combat round. Resistance takes no time whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T12:13:59-08:00","id":810726,"title":"","content":"I think perhaps we do need Eddy or someone to jump in here and tell us the intent. Perhaps this was an error? I think we can all agree that as ST's we would probably run it as an instant or as a once per turn reflexive, because it has the potential to eclipse a lot of the weapons that would be used as an instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T12:42:52-08:00","id":810748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810628#post810628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If activating the power was instant, then you would breathe fire as an instant action. The activation of the power <i>does not</i>, unlike, again, <i>later available examples</i>, provide the ability to make an attack. The activation of the power IS an attack, which is why it counts as a ranged attack, instead of - the wording you'd need for your interpretation - granting you the ability to make an attack as an instant action.<br /> <br /> It doesn't say that and it isn't meant to say that.<br /> <br /> Breathing and sweating aren't actions any more than being alive is an action. I don't ask my players to write down a list of autonomic body functions as their reflexive action for the turn and then blind them if they forgot to mention &quot;using my eyes to interpret visual data&quot; which is where you seem to be heading. Walking is movement, and movement, yes, has limitations attached. You're not limited by how many times you can resist supernatural powers, and you can't resist the same power fifty times in a turn until you succeed your roll. This is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> But if reflexives were infinite, most Beast powers have a serious problem. Does Needs Must add my Lair dots to my Perception, or an infinite amount of multiples of my Lair dots since I can keep activating it freely? Actually...why isn't that <b>Action:</b> None? I just realized every single Atavism is framed as either Reflexive or Instant, and the reflexives include clearly passive effects and bonuses. But passive effects aren't activated reflexively, they're passive. It looks like maybe this is a typo issue after all, because (by your logic) you should be able to activate any of these an infinite number of times, right? Which cannot possibly be argued to be INTENT.<br /> <br /> Either this is just action mislabeling across the board or you shouldn't be able to use the same reflexive action again and again and again and again.<br /> <br /> But I think we can all agree there's a serious problem here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can probably activate Needs Must as many times as you want. Turn if off too, but it won't stack on itself.<br /> <br /> If activating the power was the same as attacking, that means I can't just turn it on merely to shield myself without burning something. That doesn't sounds like smart design.<br /> <br /> The problem isn't that serious if someone with a bit of common sense reads it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810719#post810719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, because tanking Supernatural Powers isn't really an active response, so I'd let you do that as often as you need to. The problem is active reflexive actions, like activating powers. Remember: I said that it had to <i>reasonably </i>fit within an approximately 3 second long combat round. Resistance takes no time whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone is gonna limit reflexive actions, those are reflexive actions as well.<br /> <br /> Your arguments are very poor from where I stand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-17-2016, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:22:24-08:00","id":810780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810748#post810748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can probably activate Needs Must as many times as you want. Turn if off too, but it won't stack on itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turn it OFF? How, can you show me where that functionality is? What's its duration, exactly, that it turns off? Can you explain why you can't keep stacking it, since you can stack reflexive uses of Dragonfire to breath an infinite amount of fire? These are rhetorical, of course. What's happening is that you're writing rules text in your head and then appending it to the powers that don't work, and while this is a good skill to have an ST, it's ultimately homebrew - and a paid product shouldn't rely on it.<br /> <br /> Beast isn't published yet. Let's not start the whole Rule Zero fallacy and end up degrading the game as a result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810748#post810748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If activating the power was the same as attacking, that means I can't just turn it on merely to shield myself without burning something. That doesn't sounds like smart design.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the same as attacking. Says right in the book, &quot;counts as a ranged attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're right, that doesn't sound like smart design. It sounds like maybe this is a first-pass backer PDF with hastily-written elements that need to be called out rather than smoothed over by &quot;common sense,&quot; which as we all know, is neither common nor often sensible. In this case, requiring new players who might not have the system experience of you or I to understand they should be appending a bunch of subsidiary rules that they need to both recognize the need for and know how to implement isn't really a great way to introduce them to the new-and-improved One Book Full Rules presentation of Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810748#post810748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your arguments are very poor from where I stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where you stand doesn't make sense to me. You want infinity reflexive actions but then you want any reflexive action that actually can be used infinity times to follow special rules, but you don't think those rules need to be written, they should just be assumed. Your entire argument here is &quot;Dragonfire doesn't work the way it works, because if it did, that would be bad.&quot; That's not helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 01-17-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:47:52-08:00","id":810795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810780#post810780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where you stand doesn't make sense to me. You want infinity reflexive actions but then you want any reflexive action that actually can be used infinity times to follow special rules, but you don't think those rules need to be written, they should just be assumed. Your entire argument here is &quot;Dragonfire doesn't work the way it works, because if it did, that would be bad.&quot; That's not helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I could clarify:<br /> <br /> 1) Ephsy isn't arguing for &quot;infinite&quot; Reflexives, but that Reflexive actions need to have the ability to be used as many times in a turn as makes sense. You can only resist the supernatural mental power as often as it allows you to resist, but you need to have the ability to resist five times if five different characters all use the same power on you in the same turn. Similarly on a more active level, lots of supernaturals have active Reflexive abilities that are capped in some fashion (such as spending resource points). For example vampires can buff their physicals reflexively, and it explicitly stacks, but it isn't broken because blood isn't infinite. Capping all individual Reflexive actions to onces per turn would work directly contradict how these things are supposed to work.<br /> <br /> 2) Most of us are applying the following way of reading rules: &quot;If there is more than one way to read the rules, and one reading - even if perhaps the more correct technical parsing - is clearly stupid, don't use the stupid one.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:08:23-08:00","id":810809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810795#post810795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I could clarify:<br /> <br /> 1) Ephsy isn't arguing for &quot;infinite&quot; Reflexives, but that Reflexive actions need to have the ability to be used as many times in a turn as makes sense. You can only resist the supernatural mental power as often as it allows you to resist, but you need to have the ability to resist five times if five different characters all use the same power on you in the same turn. Similarly on a more active level, lots of supernaturals have active Reflexive abilities that are capped in some fashion (such as spending resource points). For example vampires can buff their physicals reflexively, and it explicitly stacks, but it isn't broken because blood isn't infinite. Capping all individual Reflexive actions to onces per turn would work directly contradict how these things are supposed to work.<br /> <br /> 2) Most of us are applying the following way of reading rules: &quot;If there is more than one way to read the rules, and one reading - even if perhaps the more correct technical parsing - is clearly stupid, don't use the stupid one.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Vamps can't endlessly boost their stats any more. It's capped at +2 dice per roll for a turn.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood and Smoke: the Stryx Chronicles, pp. 101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical Intensity Vampire tales speak of creatures stronger and faster than anything human. With Vitae, any Kindred can accomplish massive bursts of physical prowess. By spending a point of Vitae, he may add two dice to rolls involving his choice of Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina for the turn. This does not increase traits derived from these Attributes. However, it will increase relevant resistances. For example, a Strength increase will reduce an opponent\u2019s rolls to grapple him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your other point, I agree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T15:03:51-08:00","id":810833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810809#post810809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vamps can't endlessly boost their stats any more. It's capped at +2 dice per roll for a turn.<br /> <br /> Your other point, I agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The text you're quoting doesn't say what you're claiming it says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T15:33:18-08:00","id":810846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810833#post810833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The text you're quoting doesn't say what you're claiming it says.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he meant to quote the part that says that a Vamp can only spend so much Vitae a turn. meaning that there is a practical limit to how much you can pump yourself up regardless if the action is reflexive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T15:39:24-08:00","id":810848,"title":"","content":"It is written badly. Full stop.<br /> <br /> The correct interpretation is likely that it is a reflexive action to activate the defensive aspect of the power - that is, the immunity to fire. Defensive abilities normally need to be reflexive to make sense. The actual attack should be an instant action, but of course it is not listed as an instant action, simply a ranged one. The line should like read &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">This counts as an instant ranged attack action...&quot; instead.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T16:00:11-08:00","id":810856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810846#post810846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think he meant to quote the part that says that a Vamp can only spend so much Vitae a turn. meaning that there is a practical limit to how much you can pump yourself up regardless if the action is reflexive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was actually my point... Physical Intensity is limited by vitae/turn based on Blood Potency. When the books feel like having active reflexive powers that can be used multiple times a turn, but a cap is necessary, a cap is added to suit the mechanic. Physical Intensity and Healing are capped by how much blood you can spend. Your vampire ability to sense other vampires that can't cloak their Predatory Aura is unlimited because there's no need for it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T16:20:24-08:00","id":810866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810795#post810795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of us are applying the following way of reading rules: &quot;If there is more than one way to read the rules, and one reading - even if perhaps the more correct technical parsing - is clearly stupid, don't use the stupid one.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most of you are talking past each other in a non-argument. No one is arguing that the wrong interpretation is the correct one here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T16:49:50-08:00","id":810872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810848#post810848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is written badly. Full stop.<br /> <br /> The correct interpretation is likely that it is a reflexive action to activate the defensive aspect of the power - that is, the immunity to fire. Defensive abilities normally need to be reflexive to make sense. The actual attack should be an instant action, but of course it is not listed as an instant action, simply a ranged one. The line should like read &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">This counts as an instant ranged attack action...&quot; instead.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you are right, but the bigger problem is that this is not explicitly called out in any of the Drama &amp; Systems Chapters in any of the CoD books currently in print. A Reference table of common Action types, and a clear stance on when an action can or cannot be taken in exception to those rules needs to be included in the rules system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T18:00:50-08:00","id":810890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=810866#post810866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most of you are talking past each other in a non-argument. No one is arguing that the wrong interpretation is the correct one here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh there's plenty of talking past each other.<br /> <br /> Part of that though, is people insisting that the agreed upon &quot;wrong interpretation,&quot; is in fact the only correct way to read the rules... which gets into all of this talk about some need to modify the core rules on Reflexives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T23:45:51-08:00","id":811001,"title":"","content":"Okay so...<br /> Rather than argue with each other over this how about we try to figure out what the intent of this was? Did they intent the flame shot to be a instant action, or did they intend it to be a once per turn reflexive action, as I think that is what we have boiled it down to being the 2 most reasonable intentions. can we maybe discuss which of these we as the community agree on until we get outside help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T01:19:31-08:00","id":811035,"title":"","content":"Activating the power is reflexive. Using it to attack people (instead of it's other functions, or just looking scary because &quot;Holy crap their mouth is full of fire!&quot;) is an instant action.<br /> <br /> Reflexive single-shot attacks are part of a larger group of actions 1e allowed that multiple writers, and developers, have repeatedly said are things not intended to be part of 2e. Unless the text is 100% explicit that something would allow you to attack more than once in a turn, it should always be assumed that 2e authorial intent is for it to not allow you to do that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:35:37-08:00","id":811297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811001#post811001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so...<br /> Rather than argue with each other over this how about we try to figure out what the intent of this was? Did they intent the flame shot to be a instant action, or did they intend it to be a once per turn reflexive action, as I think that is what we have boiled it down to being the 2 most reasonable intentions. can we maybe discuss which of these we as the community agree on until we get outside help?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Heavy Arms has just demonstrated, nobody's going to agree unilaterally on what's going on here. My suspicion is that intent was originally for the attack to be a once per turn reflexive action, but that it will change to be an instant action with a passive effect (those effects need serious cleanup; &quot;always on&quot; stuff should not be modeled as reflexive) sometime during the transition from backer PDF to store PDF. That or there will be zero changes to the wording and this debate will continue forever, unremarked-upon, with various tables using it one way or another or banning the entire Atavism to avoid debate.<br /> <br /> Until official commentary comes down, I'm pretty sure that everyone's resolved on their position: either you are meant to see the hidden intent and know to write a few new lines for the power yourself such that it now requires an instant action, or the RAW is correct, and activating the power at all constitutes a ranged attack, and thus requires houseruling to make it less over-the-top powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:16:53-08:00","id":811315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811297#post811297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Heavy Arms has just demonstrated, nobody's going to agree unilaterally on what's going on here. My suspicion is that intent was originally for the attack to be a once per turn reflexive action, but that it will change to be an instant action with a passive effect (those effects need serious cleanup; &amp;quot;always on&amp;quot; stuff should not be modeled as reflexive) sometime during the transition from backer PDF to store PDF. That or there will be zero changes to the wording and this debate will continue forever, unremarked-upon, with various tables using it one way or another or banning the entire Atavism to avoid debate.<br /> <br /> Until official commentary comes down, I'm pretty sure that everyone's resolved on their position: either you are meant to see the hidden intent and know to write a few new lines for the power yourself such that it now requires an instant action, or the RAW is correct, and activating the power at all constitutes a ranged attack, and thus requires houseruling to make it less over-the-top powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of what I meant was let's just vote on it as a quorum and be done, one person from each side gives their opinion, as a closing argument then vote and we call it good till the store PDF. That seems the best way to handle this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T16:18:39-08:00","id":811361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811315#post811315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of what I meant was let's just vote on it as a quorum and be done, one person from each side gives their opinion, as a closing argument then vote and we call it good till the store PDF. That seems the best way to handle this.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but that's kind of a bizarre way to handle anything on the Internet. Voting isn't going to transition Dragonfire's activation line into an instant action, nor will pretending that it did help players who buy Beast come to an understanding they weren't already headed for. My hope is visibility for the issue, not the collected opinions of, what, five people? Who would that even help, exactly? Say we vote that RAW'S RAW and Dragonfire is reflexive despite its breaking the design aesthetic for 2E, or that it's actually a (useless) reflexive action, also breaking the design aesthetic, which serves no purpose but to allow for further instant actions. That doesn't actually help anyone in any appreciable way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T16:32:51-08:00","id":811368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811361#post811361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hope is visibility for the issue</div> </div> </div> </div>Errata's been closed since mid-November, man. If it's been caught, it's been caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T16:36:06-08:00","id":811370,"title":"","content":"I assume the reason it's reflexive is because of the immunity to fire, not because of the fire breathing, as an aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-18-2016, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T16:59:13-08:00","id":811387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811297#post811297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suspicion is that intent was originally for the attack to be a once per turn reflexive action...</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what exactly?<br /> <br /> All of writers/developers that are credited in the book that have commented on such things have been very strong on keeping multiple actions out of 2e without serious limitations/costs.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the text says anything that indicates that this power is meant to a free attack that lets you do other things. The general Atavism section even includes a description of this power as seeing someone take a deep breath before spewing out a blast of fire; not fire just puffing out in a blink of the eye.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly willing to acknowledge the writing as-is is flawed, but between the general Atavism section (both the discussion of how Atavisms generally work,and the descriptions/examples it uses), and the text of the power, there is nothing in the text supports the original intent as being a once-per-turn Reflexive attack. If the intent was to allow that, where is anything besides clumsy rules text that indicates the power is supposed to allow you to breath fire at people and do other things with your turn?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That or there will be zero changes to the wording and this debate will continue forever, unremarked-upon, with various tables using it one way or another or banning the entire Atavism to avoid debate. </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:14:45-08:00","id":811397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811361#post811361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offense, but that's kind of a bizarre way to handle anything on the Internet. Voting isn't going to transition Dragonfire's activation line into an instant action, nor will pretending that it did help players who buy Beast come to an understanding they weren't already headed for. My hope is visibility for the issue, not the collected opinions of, what, five people? Who would that even help, exactly? Say we vote that RAW'S RAW and Dragonfire is reflexive despite its breaking the design aesthetic for 2E, or that it's actually a (useless) reflexive action, also breaking the design aesthetic, which serves no purpose but to allow for further instant actions. That doesn't actually help anyone in any appreciable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been pointed out they aren't collecting errors any more. So likely the best we can do is create a fan errata. Which if this thread is noticed before printing, then they will catch it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise we can add it to a C.o.D. wiki to help future players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:42:48-08:00","id":811481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811370#post811370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason it's reflexive is because of the immunity to fire, not because of the fire breathing, as an aside.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the worst possible origin of the issue: that they made a subsidiary power that should be persistent into reflexive with no duration listing and then used that action choice for the whole thing despite it being an &quot;and by the way&quot; benefit, and then failed to note any action at all for the actual eponymous thing you're meant to do with Dragonfire. But that can't be right, that's crazy. But the RAW is crazy! But so is the concept of &quot;priming&quot; an instant action by using a reflexive action. Why? The instant action is the only part that matters. What's the reflexive doing there?<br /> <br /> It's mind-twisting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:51:09-08:00","id":811485,"title":"","content":"Okay, clarity moment: I <i>assume </i>that's why they did it. I have no idea if they did for that reason or not. My bad, i'll fix that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T20:32:26-08:00","id":811510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811481#post811481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the worst possible origin of the issue: that they made a subsidiary power that should be persistent into reflexive with no duration listing and then used that action choice for the whole thing despite it being an &quot;and by the way&quot; benefit, and then failed to note any action at all for the actual eponymous thing you're meant to do with Dragonfire. But that can't be right, that's crazy. But the RAW is crazy! But so is the concept of &quot;priming&quot; an instant action by using a reflexive action. Why? The instant action is the only part that matters. What's the reflexive doing there?<br /> <br /> It's mind-twisting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take our word for it. It makes more sense than your alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:06:26-08:00","id":811805,"title":"","content":"The alternative that the rules written are, in fact, the rules written, however ill-conceived? Looking over the stuff Beasts can do in other atavisms - reflexively become invisible and immaterial at the end of their action, making them immune to attackers not specifically delaying until they pop out for a second, chunk heal their entire Health reflexively while also gaining immunity to wound penalties and unconsciousness - I feel like it's way more likely that someone said, hey, wouldn't it be cool if they could breathe fire reflexively while doing other stuff than that they said, hey, let's say that Dragonfire is a reflexive activation that counts as a ranged attack, and trust players to know that we're lying, it actually DOESN'T count as a ranged attack but allows you to spend an instant action to MAKE one, and the reflexive activation refers to the persistent power of fire resistance despite having neither duration nor indication that if it is indeed indefinite you can even turn it off.<br /> <br /> Your claim relies on a mixture of unfamiliarity with the very rules Beast is built from <i>on the part of its builders </i>and the deliberate decision to write the power upside-down and backwards. My claim requires only that at some point someone made a decision of questionable balance, which doesn't seem so extreme alongside all the other rules Beasts can break even if it kinda actually is. I can understand a mistake like that. The one you think is &quot;reasonable&quot; to assume beggars my imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:09:17-08:00","id":811807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811805#post811805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The alternative that the rules written are, in fact, the rules written, however ill-conceived?</b> Looking over the stuff Beasts can do in other atavisms - reflexively become invisible and immaterial at the end of their action, making them immune to attackers not specifically delaying until they pop out for a second, chunk heal their entire Health reflexively while also gaining immunity to wound penalties and unconsciousness - I feel like it's way more likely that someone said, hey, wouldn't it be cool if they could breathe fire reflexively while doing other stuff than that they said, hey, let's say that Dragonfire is a reflexive activation that counts as a ranged attack, and trust players to know that we're lying, it actually DOESN'T count as a ranged attack but allows you to spend an instant action to MAKE one, and the reflexive activation refers to the persistent power of fire resistance despite having neither duration nor indication that if it is indeed indefinite you can even turn it off.<br /> <br /> Your claim relies on a mixture of unfamiliarity with the very rules Beast is built from <i>on the part of its builders </i>and the deliberate decision to write the power upside-down and backwards. My claim requires only that at some point someone made a decision of questionable balance, which doesn't seem so extreme alongside all the other rules Beasts can break even if it kinda actually is. I can understand a mistake like that. The one you think is &quot;reasonable&quot; to assume beggars my imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just assume I'm rolling on the floor with laughter at the sheer contradiction that the developers would have conned us into here, if your scenario was the slightless bit plausible (which, for the record, requires a convoluted reading of the trait in question).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-19-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:52:36-08:00","id":811886,"title":"","content":"I'll give my opinion.<br /> When they made the template for doing avatisms it was pre-filled with Reflexive and the writer forgot to change it, and it's a shame this wasn't caught before now so it could have been changed.<br /> So...<br /> First question is there an Already Existing Chronicles of Darkness Wiki?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:53:45-08:00","id":812036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811807#post811807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just assume I'm</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm sure we're both all loaded up with assumptions about the other by now.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty much done with the topic, I guess, after consideration. I'm confident in my appraisal and confident about what needs to be done. I won't give up hope that this is either in the pipeline or a candidate for last-minute sanity errata, but if not it's hardly a dealbreaker. At this point probably everything worth saying has been said at least twice, and no one thinks it SHOULD be a reflexive action, so regardless of whether we consider ourself seers of developer intent or compensatory houserulers we're at least unanimous on that front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:01:00-08:00","id":812042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=811805#post811805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative that the rules written are, in fact, the rules written, however ill-conceived?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is arguing that the RAW are phrased poorly. However reading the Dragonfire rules out of context with the general Atavism write-up is wrong. Phrases such as:<br /> <br /> &quot;The witness sees the Eshmaki take a deep breath and then exhale a gout of blue fire,...&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Many Atavisms resemble Merits in that they have persistent effects that need not be activated, such as modifying other actions or dice pools, or they confer abilities that are available at no cost, such as a special attack form. Dice rolls are rarely required. When they are, they are usually reflexive and folded into another action such an attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> cannot be ignored.<br /> <br /> Which you have to ignore to claim that the RAW unambiguously allow reflexive fire-breath attacks, because those are part of the rules, not just the Dragonfire write-up. The second part especially reads to make it clear that Dragonfire reflexively creates the ability to make fire-breath attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Looking over the stuff Beasts can do in other atavisms - reflexively become invisible and immaterial at the end of their action, making them immune to attackers not specifically delaying until they pop out for a second, chunk heal their entire Health reflexively while also gaining immunity to wound penalties and unconsciousness - I feel like it's way more likely that someone said, hey, wouldn't it be cool if they could breathe fire reflexively while doing other stuff than that they said, hey, let's say that Dragonfire is a reflexive activation that counts as a ranged attack, and trust players to know that we're lying, it actually DOESN'T count as a ranged attack but allows you to spend an instant action to MAKE one, and the reflexive activation refers to the persistent power of fire resistance despite having neither duration nor indication that if it is indeed indefinite you can even turn it off. </div> </div> </div>Costless Reflexive attacks are infinitely more potent than other Atavisms.<br /> <br /> ST: Combat starts.<br /> Eshmaki Player: I reflexive declare 1,000 fire attacks on every enemy within 15 yards.<br /> ST: I'm not rolling that shit, ok, everything without fire immunity dies.<br /> <br /> That's what costless reflexive attacks means. It also makes the low Satiety version pointless. Who needs burst fire when you can infinitely attack everyone?<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're trying to claim that the intent is for it to be one reflexive attack per turn... cite me anything in any of the relevant books, or any creator posts anywhere, that support that. Because nothing in the text says that. The only options the RAW allow are:<br /> <br /> 1) The general Atavaism section does, in fact, mean that Dragonfire should be read as reflexively creating the ability to make fire-breath attacks.<br /> 2) Dragonfire allows infinite attacks.<br /> <br /> &quot;One reflexive attack per turn,&quot; has no basis in any rules I can find on the subject. Your claim requires reading something in <i>that is absolutely nowhere in the book</i>, rather than picking one of two interpretations from the text.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:36:46-08:00","id":812067,"title":"","content":"I actually don't have to ignore your lines-such-as; I can take them into account and then simply see Dragonfire as a specific and deliberate exception. But it comes to the same end, doesn't it? It needs to be an instant action. Yes? I do not mistake your position? Does anyone feel it would be <i>of no benefit</i> to just note that Dragonfire is an instant action regardless of what you think the <i>intent</i> was?<br /> <br /> I also don't think I need to go over your reflexive infinity thing again. Or at least I hoped I wouldn't, but here we are. It isn't an explicit rule that you cannot activate a given reflexive anything (ANYTHING) more than once on your turn; fine! Like you say, Dragonfire and Needs Must and Cyclopean Strength and whatever else can be used infinitely for infinite damage or infinite dice if you assume that the lack of an explicit ruling is the same as permission. So it needs to be an explicit rule! Okay! I'm on board with that! Just stick it right in the definition of a reflexive action, you cannot normally perform a particular reflexive action more than once because <i>that's insane</i>. But I think at least half the problem is the repeated use of &quot;reflexive&quot; where &quot;reflexive&quot; is not, in fact, what makes sense and &quot;persistent&quot; or &quot;instant&quot; or maybe just providing some kind of separation when you have one action line for multiple powers to avoid this exact issue. Will it be fixed, who knows, maybe not, but I'm not arguing that it <i>should be that way</i>.<br /> <br /> You keep saying what equates to &quot;if this worked the way you say it did, it would be ridiculous&quot; as a two-part argument - it would be therefore it isn't - and you're missing the part that I agree with that statement, I'm just saying it does therefore it IS. I'm not assigning a positive value to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:17:36-08:00","id":812167,"title":"","content":"Or you can perform the action as many times as your want (being reflexive) - just, it's benefits do not stack over itself anymore that tachycardia would for being an improvement for normal breathing. Attacks, being attacks, clearly can't apply to that (Because by setting and mechanical standard, they must be Instant). Otherwise we enter the realm of shonen silliness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5SjhydTcL4\" data-code=\"J5SjhydTcL4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/J5SjhydTcL4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:30:22-08:00","id":812180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=812067#post812067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't have to ignore your lines-such-as; I can take them into account and then simply see Dragonfire as a specific and deliberate exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you can cite anything that Dragonfire is supposed to be an exception, this has no weight to it. I also don't see how you can stand by an interpretation that comes down to, &quot;I think Dragonfire is a specific and deliberate exception to something written about Dragonfire.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does anyone feel it would be <i>of no benefit</i> to just note that Dragonfire is an instant action regardless of what you think the <i>intent</i> was? </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be of benefit because nobody is arguing that all of Dragonfire should be an instant action. But there would be rather major benefit to noting that the attack option with Dragonfire is an instant action... because then this argument wouldn't exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't think I need to go over your reflexive infinity thing again. Or at least I hoped I wouldn't, but here we are. </div> </div> </div>That happens when your arguments basically revolve around repeating how right you clearly think you are, and how you don't need to actually do things like cite the books or anything like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't an explicit rule that you cannot activate a given reflexive anything (ANYTHING) more than once on your turn; fine! Like you say, Dragonfire and Needs Must and Cyclopean Strength and whatever else can be used infinitely for infinite damage or infinite dice if you assume that the lack of an explicit ruling is the same as permission. </div> </div> </div>Activating a power infinite times is not the same as being able to stack it. Activating a reflexive dice-adder simply ends the first use and starts the second use. Or as the devs usually just say, &quot;no these don't stack.&quot; That's why reflexive attacks are dangerous. Attacks aren't dice tricks, they're full actions. Re-activating a reflexive dice bonus is not the same as re-activating a reflexive attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just stick it right in the definition of a reflexive action, you cannot normally perform a particular reflexive action more than once because <i>that's insane</i>. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. We've addressed this. And as I noted above, most &quot;infinite&quot; reflexives aren't a probably because they don't stack in a meaningful fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You keep saying what equates to &quot;if this worked the way you say it did, it would be ridiculous&quot; as a two-part argument - it would be therefore it isn't - and you're missing the part that I agree with that statement, I'm just saying it does therefore it IS. I'm not assigning a positive value to that. </div> </div> </div>No. The two parts are:<br /> <br /> 1) The way you're saying is the intent is still ridiculous.<br /> 2) The way you're insisting on your position on what the &quot;RAW&quot; is, is a tortured mess of nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:27:06-08:00","id":812237,"title":"","content":"Most of what you've said, I'll admit, I think is badly wrong or badly confused, if including elements of truth, or both. Buuut...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=812180#post812180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be of benefit because nobody is arguing that all of Dragonfire should be an instant action. But there would be rather major benefit to noting that the attack option with Dragonfire is an instant action... because then this argument wouldn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you agree with me, despite your need to first state that you don't agree with me! Fantastic! I have no interest in pursuing any of this any further with you. I feel that we have reached accord on both the only thing we're going to, and the only thing that matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:05:12-08:00","id":812286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=812237#post812237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of what you've said, I'll admit, I think is badly wrong or badly confused, if including elements of truth, or both. Buuut...</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of thing? Were you just say to someone that disagrees with you, &quot;You're wrong because I say so. I don't have to explain how so, I don't have to explain why, I don't have to back it up. I just have to declare you wrong so you are!&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what leads to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have no interest in pursuing any of this any further with you. </div> </div> </div>Because it makes it pretty clear you never really had any interest in anything other than people agreeing with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:57:09-08:00","id":812329,"title":"","content":"Would you feel more positively inclined towards my motives if I responded to your point-for-point in its entirety so we could keep it going for another six pages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:09:44-08:00","id":812339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=812167#post812167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can perform the action as many times as your want (being reflexive) - just, it's benefits do not stack over itself anymore that tachycardia would for being an improvement for normal breathing. Attacks, being attacks, clearly can't apply to that (Because by setting and mechanical standard, they must be Instant). Otherwise we enter the realm of shonen silliness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5SjhydTcL4\" data-code=\"J5SjhydTcL4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/J5SjhydTcL4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I think a good rule of thumb might be...if It pushes broken in Exalted, it doesn't belong in C.o.D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T21:24:14-08:00","id":812377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=812329#post812329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you feel more positively inclined towards my motives if I responded to your point-for-point in its entirety so we could keep it going for another six pages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I don't care about the format of your response. I care about if you're going to engage in a discussion in good faith, and actually address what people say in a meaningful sense.<br /> <br /> The fact that you're &quot;done&quot; with this conversation, except to come back to snark at me, doesn't really convince me that you ever cared about doing anything other than making it clear that people that don't agree with you will be treated poorly in lieu of responding to valid points they make.<br /> <br /> I don't think it is all the complicated. Saying, repeatedly, that you feel this conversation is pointless, and instead of just dropping it, and then coming back in to respond with repetitions of how obviously right you are, and then how much a dick that justifies being, isn't doing you any favors.<br /> <br /> Now, if you respond to be previous points in good faith, and drop the passive aggressive crap for a few posts? Yeah, that would improve my impressions of your motives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T22:09:51-08:00","id":812389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=812167#post812167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can perform the action as many times as your want (being reflexive) - just, it's benefits do not stack over itself anymore that tachycardia would for being an improvement for normal breathing. Attacks, being attacks, clearly can't apply to that (Because by setting and mechanical standard, they must be Instant). Otherwise we enter the realm of shonen silliness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5SjhydTcL4\" data-code=\"J5SjhydTcL4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/J5SjhydTcL4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I think, for those who desire that sort of game, a system hack would be a reasonable option. Might just have to write one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T01:08:24-08:00","id":812434,"title":"","content":"Go play Exalted if you want that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T01:52:41-08:00","id":812447,"title":"","content":"Or at least a bit less negatively: Recognize that the CofD is a really bad base system to try to build that sort of game. Hacking it to turn it into that... is vastly more effort that it is probably worth compared to taking games that are closer to that and making them more like whatever draws you to the CofD systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:54:12-08:00","id":812648,"title":"","content":"*shrug* YMMV","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T04:00:14-08:00","id":814029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/779050-dragonfire-mechanics-wait-it-s-reflexive?p=812434#post812434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go play Exalted if you want that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't work like that in Exalted either. That's twice now I've seen you be nasty to people of a particular fanbase -From a WoD/Chronicles of Darkness/Exalted/Trinity fan.<br /> <br /> As much as I like to think that rules can be laid out so that a rules lawyer wont attempt to exploit some aspect of it. Experience has taught me that people looking for exploits are generally going to find them. Which if that is the case I would wonder aloud to those people about what their motivations playing an rpg are. So baring the writers wanting to give Beasts an insanely overpowered attack or gleefully cackling as they watch their carefully placed power and it's working be abused. I'm liable to think the more sane answers about it providing a new type of attack you might otherwise not have available to you, like using your action in a combat round to blast a gout of fire. Well that saner answer might just MIGHT be the far more plausible one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:59:07-08:00","id":814077,"title":"","content":"You're reading a tone in my post that it entirely lacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:59:19-08:00","id":814339,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bIt wasn't nasty, but it wasn't helpful either. Not without additional context. Without the additional context it's thread crapping. I'm not about to issue a sanction, but other mods might not be so patient, so please be more aware of how your posts are coming across to other people.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T14:15:57-08:00","id":814449,"title":"","content":"Activating Dragonfire is reflexive, but making an attack is an instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.d